  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved the best accuracy (0.650) so far, while config_037 (same but multimodal with resnet50, avgpool, concat) scored lower (0.632), suggesting the image branch with resnet50 is a weak or even detrimental signal in the multiprofile regime. The aggregation method (avgpool) has only been tested in one configuration, leaving open whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) could further improve the multiprofile representation. Question: config_007 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002, isolating the effect of aggregation (transformer vs. avgpool) while holding model setting, profile, and encoder constant. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests whether the 0.650 ceiling is due to avgpool being suboptimal or whether the multiprofile+scvi_n200 representation is already near its limit. If transformer helps, it informs all future multimodal experiments; if not, we can confidently keep avgpool and redirect budget toward improving the image encoder or fusion strategy. This avoids confounding multiple design choices and reduces uncertainty about a core architectural decision before investing in more complex multimodal variants."
}

